3. What happens after attention?
The attention output is passed through the rest of the Transformer block. The model repeats these operations across many layers, progressively transforming the token representations.

Eventually, the final representations are used to calculate scores for possible next tokens. During text generation, the model uses those scores to select or sample the next token.

Interview-ready answer: The attention output is the weighted combination of Value vectors, based on Query–Key attention scores.
It gives each token a context-enriched representation, which subsequent Transformer layers use to process context and ultimately generate text.
