The attention mechanism in a Transformer helps each token build a context-aware representation by incorporating information from other relevant tokens.
Query, Key, and Value calculations help a Transformer produce a contextual representation of each token.

Query (Q) and Key (K): Calculate how relevant other permitted tokens are to the current token.
Softmax: Converts the scores into attention weights.
Value (V): Supplies the information that gets combined using those weights.
Attention output: Produces the updated, context-enriched representation of the token.

