what is attention mask?

An attention mask tells a Transformer which token positions it is allowed to pay attention to and which positions it must ignore.

Query and Key vectors
|
Calculate attention scores
|
Apply attention mask
Block prohibited positions
|
Softmax → attention weights
|
Weighted combination of Value vectors
|
Attention output

Interview-ready answer
“An attention mask controls which positions a token can attend to. In causal self-attention, the mask prevents future-token information from influencing the current position. In padding masks, it prevents attention to padding tokens. 
The mask is applied to attention scores before Softmax, making prohibited positions receive zero attention weight.”


Remember: Q and K calculate relevance, the mask controls which positions are permitted, Softmax produces attention weights, and V provides the information combined to form the attention output.
